	This may or may not be my record, but I, at least, remember it pretty 
well (and still have the notes from that game, more importantly).

	My third ascension, a wishless orc barbarian, found three bones 
levels... one single, one double, and one triple.

	The single was my immediately-prior orc barbarian, killed by a mob of 
fire ants on DL4. Despite lack of fire resistance, he got all but one of 
them before the last one got him, and my next character had an easy time 
with the survivor, and scored Cleaver from the bones.

	The double was in Mine Town... a couple of mummies, one of them a 
seriously badass valkyrie who'd gotten blindsided by an ettin mummy, and 
the other a neutral human barbarian who took down the ettin before I 
realized where I was and proceeded to get 0wn3d by the valk while 
running for the stairs. Getting rid of those two was not at all easy... 
I went down the stairs, recognized the level, and tucked my tail between 
my legs and ran back up the stairs, didn't come back for a good long 
while. When I did, I still came closer than I liked to getting taken out 
by the valkyrie.

	The triple was two rogues and a wizard, in Delphi (on DL5). I'm not 
sure what killed any of them; they were in hallways, so didn't leave 
gravestones, and I lost enough hapless squishies in that period that I 
don't recall those particular ones (though I have a vague recollection 
that one of the rogues went down to "I have a powerful artifact 
weapon... pity about the crappy AC and meager HP" overconfidence). I 
didn't run into anything particularly tough on that level, but "tough" 
for a barbarian and "tough" for an rogue or wizard are two different 
things. Scored Stormbringer off one of the rogues, and ultimately 
ascended with it my hand. I also got a bag of holding from her, but, 
after complex shenanigans to get it de-cursed, I managed to blow it up 
with a typo... put an identified wand of cancellation into it thinking I 
was putting it into my storage chest. Fortunately, there was nothing 
vital in it. Unfortunately, that was the only bag of holding I saw the 
entire game. The hassle of picking equipment for the final ascension run 
without a BoH was the only thing that made me regret my wishless 
conduct. Though, on the bright side, with just a plain ol' sack, the 
malignant auras were much less threatening.

